@startuml PayLink_Payment_State_Diagram
!theme plain
hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
  BorderColor #333333
  FontSize 14
}
skinparam arrow {
  Color #333333
  FontSize 12
}

title PayLink — Payment State Diagram

' Initial state
[*] --> Initiated

' Transitions from the brief
Initiated --> FundsHeld : Fraud checks pass\nand wallet has enough funds
Initiated --> Rejected : Fraud check fails or\nfunds are insufficient

FundsHeld --> SentToBiller : Request sent to biller

SentToBiller --> Completed : Biller confirms
SentToBiller --> Failed : Biller refuses
SentToBiller --> Unknown : No answer within the timeout

Unknown --> Completed : Biller later confirms\n(callback, retry or settlement file)
Unknown --> Failed : Biller later refuses, or\nreconciliation finds no payment

Failed --> Refunded : Hold released to the wallet

' Final states (brief states Completed, Rejected, and Refunded are final)
Completed --> [*]
Rejected --> [*]
Refunded --> [*]

' Business Rule Note
note right of Unknown
  **Crucial Business Rule:**
  A payment in Unknown is NEVER refunded automatically.
  It must transition to Failed first.
  Money is only returned once the system is sure 
  the biller did not receive it.
end note

@enduml